 The maximum kinetic energy of a beta particle is related to the nuclear mass of the nuclide through the expression;
$$KE_{max} = T_{1/2} \Delta E$$

By finding the half-life and plugging it into this equation, we get $$T_{1/2} = 16 \mu s$$ and \(\Delta E = 1.19MeV\). The answer is (B).
